; Runs the whole-model WebAssembly module [Loop_bundle_wasm] emits, in-process,
; under js_of_ocaml only: the module is generated by the same OCaml compiler
; that is running as JavaScript, so no external compiler is involved, and it is
; executed through the host's own [WebAssembly] object (node, a browser, a
; worker).
;
; JS-only by construction, like [loop_js_exec]: it calls [caml_js_*] primitives
; a native executable lacks, so it links into a (modes js) executable or an
; (inline_tests (modes js)) suite and nowhere else, though it still BUILDS
; natively. The pure generator is backend-neutral; this library and
; [loop_js_exec] are the only ones that may name js_of_ocaml for their backend.

(library
 (name loop_wasm_host)
 (libraries err_trace fmt js_of_ocaml loop_ir loop_js_exec native wasm_ir))
